C03: a reply that opens with the observed package identifier keeps its lowercase spelling (PIP1821)

PIP1819 measured: the true drafts «requests ya está instalado en Python 3.12.10 (2.32.4)…» were vetoed three times by the initial-capital rule because they begin with the package name as the person wrote it. The lowercase check now exempts a reply that opens with an observed identifier (seen.package, name, title or query written in lowercase).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


